config BR2_PACKAGE_IOEXAMPLE2
    bool "Example2: Button-controlled LED with GPIO cdev v2"
    help
      This package demonstrates GPIO input and output through the Linux
      GPIO character-device v2 API.

      The program configures one GPIO line as input (e.g., connected to the
      STM32F429 Discovery board's user button) and another GPIO line as output
      (e.g., connected to the red LED). It continuously reads the button state
      and reflects it directly on the unclaimed green LED GPIO: the LED turns ON when the button is
      pressed and OFF otherwise.

      The loop runs until the user presses any key in the terminal.
